# services/ingestion's own `.env` (gitignored) -- copy this file to
# `.env` and fill in real values. `Settings` (app/core/config.py) is a
# deliberate *subset* of data-pipeline's -- Postgres here is for
# `meta._ingest_log` writes only (never `raw.*`), and there's no
# MLflow/ML config at all (services/ingestion/TODO.md's Phase 0
# "scoped configuration" decision).

# PostgreSQL -- same instance data-pipeline points at today (Phase 0's
# recorded decision: no separate ingestion database yet). Required -- no
# working default outside this repo's own docker-compose `postgres`
# service.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/ecolens

# Second, separate Postgres instance (2026-08-12) for the real "logger"
# tables this service writes that dbt never needs to read
# (`meta._feature_selection_log` only, for this service). An explicit
# split from DATABASE_URL so high-write-volume audit/history tables
# don't share connections/load with the primary warehouse database.
# Optional -- falls back to DATABASE_URL when unset. **`meta._ingest_log`
# and `meta.anomalies` deliberately stay on DATABASE_URL, not here** --
# real correction the same day this was introduced: `meta.anomalies` is
# a live dbt *source* (`services/waerehouse/dbt/ecolens/models/staging/
# stg_anomalies.sql`, feeding the dashboard's anomaly-detection overview
# chart), and dbt's own connection profile has no knowledge of
# `LOG_DB_URL` at all -- moving that table here made the chart
# permanently stale the moment it happened, confirmed live. `meta.
# _ingest_log` stayed with it only because `meta.anomalies.run_id` has a
# real foreign key into it, not because it has its own dbt dependency.
# See `app.service.datasources.service.fetch_run_rows`'s own docstring
# for the fuller story. Every *other* audit-log table `services/
# waerehouse`/`services/forecast-api` write (`_training_log`, `_dbt_
# build_log`, `_marts_archive_log`, `_retention_log`) has no dbt-source
# dependency and correctly belongs on this same LOG_DB_URL -- set the
# identical value across all three services once deployed independently.
# LOG_DB_URL=postgresql://user:password@log-host:5432/ecolens_logs

# Redis -- circuit-breaker state + the backfill lock (Phase 1). Same
# shared instance data-pipeline uses.
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

# RabbitMQ -- publish-only (Phase 1's `publish_landed_event`). Same
# shared instance/queue data-pipeline publishes to.
RABBITMQ_URL=amqp://guest:guest@localhost:5672/

# The landed-event queue this service publishes to -- the ONE real
# coupling point with `services/waerehouse`'s own consumer
# (`consume_landed_events` reads this exact same queue name off its own
# `RABBITMQ_LANDING_QUEUE`; see that service's own `.env.example` for the
# matching side). Must be set to the identical value on both services
# once they're deployed independently -- a mismatch here doesn't error,
# it just means warehouse silently never sees this service's events
# (each side is reading/writing a queue the other was never pointed at).
# RABBITMQ_LANDING_QUEUE=ecolens.landing

# Shadow-run variant of the queue above (Phase 4's "Execute Shadow
# Runs", `--triggered-by shadow`) -- only needs to match
# `services/waerehouse`'s own value if that service's shadow-run
# tooling is also deployed and pointed at this instance; otherwise
# leave unset.
# RABBITMQ_LANDING_QUEUE_SHADOW=ecolens.landing.shadow

# OpenElectricity / BoM (optional -- anonymous/rate-limited access
# without these; needed once Phase 1 ports the 5 ingest tasks).
# OE_API_KEY=
# BOM_API_KEY=

# Cloudflare R2 (Phase 2, "Integrate Cloudflare R2 Staging") -- staged
# run files upload here under `staging/`, same account/bucket
# data-pipeline's own object_storage.py uses for assets/MLflow
# artifacts. Falls back to local MinIO (this repo's own docker-compose
# `minio` service, defaults baked into Settings) when unset.
# CLOUDFLARESTORAGE_ACCOUNT_ID=
# CLOUDFLARESTORAGE_S3_API=
# CLOUDFLARESTORAGE_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# CLOUDFLARESTORAGE_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# JWT bearer auth, verification-only (`app.core.security`) -- NOT
# currently wired into any route ("no auth required for now" -- every
# `/v1/data-sources*` endpoint is open). Left here, unused, so it's a
# one-line `Depends(require_roles(...))` change to re-enable later, not
# a re-port. This service never issues tokens itself; set JWT_SECRET to
# the same value as data-pipeline's own so a token that service issued
# via `POST /v1/auth/token` would verify here too, if/when this is
# re-wired.
# JWT_SECRET=dev-secret-change-me-32-bytes-min
# JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256
# IAM_JWT_SECRET=
# IAM_JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256
# RATE_LIMIT_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE=60
